[57.293099, "i", "cat /app/task/instruction.md\n"]
[57.29355, "o", "cat /app/task/instruction.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[57.293925, "o", "# Post-Compromise Forensic Investigation and Remediation Planning\r\n\r\nYou are a DFIR analyst working on an **analysis machine** — **not** the compromised server.\r\nA read-only forensic copy of the host is mounted at `/disk`, and the output of the\r\nsecurity product (alerts, vulnerability scan, baseline checks) is at `/sas`.\r\n\r\n## Scenario\r\n\r\nAn Ubuntu 22.04 Jenkins controller was exploited through CVE-2024-23897. The attacker dropped a cryptominer, planted a Groovy init hook and an SSH authorized_keys backdoor, added a cron job, and truncated the Jenkins log. Alerts surface the miner and the cron job; the Groovy hook and the SSH key are silent.\r\n\r\n## Rules (load-bearing — do not violate)\r\n\r\n"]
[57.293943, "o", "- You are on an analysis machine, not the compromised host.\r\n- `/disk` is a **read-only** forensic copy. Do not attempt to modify it.\r\n- Do **not** SSH into any machine or execute remediation — you are producing a plan, not\r\n  running it.\r\n- Every finding must be based on evidence in `/disk` or `/sas`."]
[57.29417, "o", "\r\n- Do **not** fabricate CVEs. State confidence levels when unsure.\r\n- In the remediation plan, prefer backup/quarantine over deletion.\r\n\r\n## Evidence is messy and multi-format\r\n\r\nReal disks are not clean text. Evidence is spread across log files, CSV/TSV tables, JSON\r\ntelemetry, config files, registry hives, `.evtx` event logs, inert binary samples, and\r\nmarkup — some of it rotated, gzipped, truncated at a cleared window, or partially\r\noverwritten. Use the right tool: `grep`/`rg`, `strings` (and `strings -e l` for UTF-16 in\r\nhives/event logs), `zcat` for `*.gz`, `jq` for JSON, `xxd` for raw bytes, `pdftotext` for\r\nPDFs. Indicators of compromise in provided intel are **defanged** (`hxxp://`, `evil[.]com`,\r\n`stratum+tcp[:]//`) — re-fang them mentally when correlating.\r\n\r\nBesides `/disk` (the host image) and the machine-readable feeds in `/sas`,\r\n`/sas` also carries analyst materials: `/sas/cti/` — a vendor threat advisory\r\n(text, PDF, and page-image PNGs) mapping the campaign to MITRE ATT&CK techniques and any\r\nrelevant CVEs; and `/sas/handoff/` — a **pre-filled change ticket with stale/incorrect\r\nentries to reconcile in place**, a findings JSON schema, and an incident intake form. Map your\r\non-disk findings to the advisory's ATT&CK claims, and correct the change ticket against your\r\nown evidence rather than trusting it.\r\n\r\n## Citations (required)\r\n\r\nEvery finding in every report must be followed by a **backtick-delimited** citation of the\r\nform `` `/absolute/path` `` or `` `/absolute/path:line` `` pointing at evidence under\r\n`/disk` **or** `/sas`. Use `/sas` for findings whose only evidence is\r\nan alert — e.g. a network connection, or an event whose primary log was wiped. **Findings\r\nwithout a resolvable citation will not be credited.**\r\n\r\n## Deliverables\r\n\r\nWrite all five files to `/app`. A run that produces fewer than five is scored as\r\nincomplete, not as a low score.\r\n\r\n| File | Content |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `progress.md` | Investigation timeline and working checklist |\r\n| `intrusion-report.md` | Attack chain, evidence, entities, persistence, impact |\r\n| `vuln-report.md` | Vulnerability-driven entry analysis (or its explicit absence) |\r\n| `baseline-report.md` | Baseline / configuration weaknesses |\r\n| `remediation-plan.md` | Prioritised, correct, complete, verifiable plan |\r\n\r\nDetection and remediation are scored on **separate** axes. Investigate the whole host — the\r\nalerts do not cover everything that happened.\r\n"]
[57.294832, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[57.295092, "o", "root@2e703238ddb6:/app# "]
[73.592685, "i", "cat /app/task/instruction.md\n"]
[73.593175, "o", "cat /app/task/instruction.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[73.593455, "o", "# Post-Compromise Forensic Investigation and Remediation Planning"]
[73.593617, "o", "\r\n\r\nYou are a DFIR analyst working on an **analysis machine** — **not** the compromised server.\r\nA read-only forensic copy of the host is mounted at `/disk`, and the output of the\r\nsecurity product (alerts, vulnerability scan, baseline checks) is at `/sas`.\r\n\r\n## Scenario\r\n\r\nAn Ubuntu 22.04 Jenkins controller was exploited through CVE-2024-23897. The attacker dropped a cryptominer, planted a Groovy init hook and an SSH authorized_keys backdoor, added a cron job, and truncated the Jenkins log. Alerts surface the miner and the cron job; the Groovy hook and the SSH key are silent.\r\n\r\n## Rules (load-bearing — do not violate)\r\n\r\n- You are on an analysis machine, not the compromised host.\r\n- `/disk` is a **read-only** forensic copy. Do not attempt to modify it.\r\n- Do **not** SSH into any machine or execute remediation — you are producing a plan, not\r\n  running it.\r\n- Every finding must be based on evidence in `/disk` or `/sas`.\r\n- Do **not** fabricate CVEs. State confidence levels when unsure.\r\n- In the remediation plan, prefer backup/quarantine over deletion.\r\n"]
[73.593855, "o", "\r\n## Evidence is messy and multi-format\r\n\r\nReal disks are not clean text. Evidence is spread across log files, CSV/TSV tables, JSON\r\ntelemetry, config files, registry hives, `.evtx` event logs, inert binary samples, and\r\nmarkup — some of it rotated, gzipped, truncated at a cleared window, or partially\r\noverwritten. Use the right tool: `grep`/`rg`, `strings` (and `strings -e l` for UTF-16 in\r\nhives/event logs), `zcat` for `*.gz`, `jq` for JSON, `xxd` for raw bytes, `pdftotext` for\r\nPDFs. Indicators of compromise in provided intel are **defanged** (`hxxp://`, `evil[.]com`,\r\n`stratum+tcp[:]//`) — re-fang them mentally when correlating.\r\n\r\nBesides `/disk` (the host image) and the machine-readable feeds in `/sas`,\r\n`/sas` also carries analyst materials: `/sas/cti/` — a vendor threat advisory\r\n(text, PDF, and page-image PNGs) mapping the campaign to MITRE ATT&CK techniques and any\r\nrelevant CVEs; and `/sas/handoff/` — a **pre-filled change ticket with stale/incorrect\r\nentries to reconcile in place**, a findings JSON schema, and an incident intake form. Map your\r\non-disk findings to the advisory's ATT&CK claims, and correct the change ticket against your\r\nown evidence rather than trusting it.\r\n\r\n## Citations (required)\r\n\r\nEvery finding in every report must be followed by a **backtick-delimited** citation of the\r\nform `` `/absolute/path` `` or `` `/absolute/path:line` `` pointing at evidence under\r\n`/disk` **or** `/sas`. Use `/sas` for findings whose only evidence is\r\nan alert — e.g. a network connection, or an event whose primary log was wiped. **Findings\r\nwithout a resolvable citation will not be credited.**\r\n\r\n## Deliverables\r\n\r\nWrite all five files to `/app`. A run that produces fewer than five is scored as\r\nincomplete, not as a low score.\r\n\r\n| File | Content |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `progress.md` | Investigation timeline and working checklist |\r\n| `intrusion-report.md` | Attack chain, evidence, entities, persistence, impact |\r\n| `vuln-report.md` | Vulnerability-driven entry analysis (or its explicit absence) |\r\n| `baseline-report.md` | Baseline / configuration weaknesses |\r\n| `remediation-plan.md` | Prioritised, correct, complete, verifiable plan |\r\n\r\nDetection and remediation are scored on **separate** axes. Investigate the whole host — the\r\nalerts do not cover everything that happened.\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@2e703238ddb6:/app# "]
[87.874335, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/check-result.json\n{\n  \"verifiable\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n    \"explanation\": \"The verifier is programmatic, deterministic, and runs locally without network access.\"\n  },\n  \"solvable\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n    \"explanation\": \"A working oracle solution is provided in solution/solve.sh that passes the test suite.\"\n  },\n  \"difficult\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n    \"explanation\": \"Requires expert knowledge of DFIR, log analysis, ATT&CK mapping, and remediation planning.\"\n  },\n  \"interesting\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n    \"explanation\": \"Simulates a realistic post-compromise digital forensics and incident response scenario.\"\n  },\n  \"outcome_verified\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n    \"explanation\": \"Tests verify the final report deliverables without dictating specific tools or step-by-step procedures.\"\n  },\n  \"anti_cheat_robustness\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n    \"explanation\": \"Ground-truth manifest resides in tests/ and cannot be modified by agent at runtime.\"\n  },\n  \"task_security\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n    \"explanation\": \"All task files are clean and free of malicious code or credential exfiltration.\"\n  },\n  \"functional_verification\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n    \"explanation\": \"Verifier parses report contents, checks citations, validates attack chain topology, and checks remediation coverage.\"\n  },\n  \"deterministic_reproducible\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n    \"explanation\": \"All data is bundled locally and verification is fully deterministic across runs.\"\n  },\n  \"essential_difficulty\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n    \"explanation\": \"Difficulty lies in host forensics, evidence correlation, and plan formulation.\"\n  },\n  \"test_instruction_alignment\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n    \"explanation\": \"Every test assertion matches requirements specified in instruction.md.\"\n  },\n  \"novel\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n    \"explanation\": \"Uses a custom synthetic forensic disk image and multi-stage attack scenario.\"\n  },\n  \"agentic\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n    \"explanation\": \"Requires multi-step terminal interaction to explore the filesystem, inspect logs, decode artifacts, and author reports.\"\n  },\n  \"reviewable\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n    \"explanation\": \"The verification logic and ground-truth manifest are clear and reviewable.\"\n  },\n  \"instruction_concision\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"fail\",\n    \"explanation\": \"Instruction explicitly lists recommended CLI tools (grep/rg, strings, zcat, jq, xxd, pdftotext) that the agent should discover on its own.\"\n  },\n  \"solution_quality\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"fail\",\n    \"explanation\": \"solution/solve.sh uses heredocs to directly write the final pre-computed markdown deliverables without performing any computation or investigation script.\"\n  },\n  \"separate_verifier_configured\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"fail\",\n    \"explanation\": \"task.toml lacks environment_mode = 'separate' and artifacts definitions, and tests/Dockerfile is missing.\"\n  },\n  \"environment_hygiene\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"fail\",\n    \"explanation\": \"tests/Dockerfile is missing so test dependencies and verifier runtime are not properly encapsulated.\"\n  },\n  \"structured_data_schema\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"not_applicable\",\n    \"explanation\": \"The task asks for human-readable markdown reports rather than structured output (JSON/CSV/API).\"\n  },\n  \"typos\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n    \"explanation\": \"No typos found in file paths, commands, or critical identifiers.\"\n  },\n  \"difficulty_explanation_quality\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"fail\",\n    \"explanation\": \"The difficulty_explanation field is missing from metadata in task.toml.\"\n  },\n  \"solution_explanation_quality\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"fail\",\n    \"explanation\": \"The solution_explanation field is missing from metadata in task.toml.\"\n  },\n  \"verification_explanation_quality\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"fail\",\n    \"explanation\": \"The verification_explanation field is missing from metadata in task.toml.\"\n  },\n  \"category_and_tags\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"fail\",\n    \"explanation\": \"The subcategory field is missing from metadata in task.toml.\"\n  },\n  \"task_name\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"fail\",\n    \"explanation\": \"task.toml defin"]
[87.874542, "i", "es name = 'dfir-eval/jenkins-groovy', which contains a slash and namespace prefix instead of a 3-word kebab-case folder slug.\"\n  },\n  \"resource_configuration\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n    \"explanation\": \"Timeouts and resource configurations are appropriate for forensic analysis.\"\n  },\n  \"task_readme\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n    \"explanation\": \"environment/README.md provides helpful context regarding disk building.\"\n  },\n  \"expert_time_estimate\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"fail\",\n    \"explanation\": \"The expert_time_estimate_hours field is missing from metadata in task.toml.\"\n  },\n  \"task_toml_schema\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"fail\",\n    \"explanation\": \"task.toml contains an unrecognized field 'difficulty = \\\"hard\\\"' in [metadata] and lacks required metadata fields.\"\n  },\n  \"no_extraneous_files\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"fail\",\n    \"explanation\": \"The task directory contains extraneous, unreferenced directories: assets/ and baselines/.\"\n  },\n  \"artifact_efficiency\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"not_applicable\",\n    \"explanation\": \"Separate verifier mode is not configured.\"\n  },\n  \"verifier_execution_isolation\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"not_applicable\",\n    \"explanation\": \"The verifier only parses text/markdown files and does not execute code produced by the agent.\"\n  },\n  \"ctrf_reporting\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"fail\",\n    \"explanation\": \"The test harness does not output CTRF results to /logs/verifier/ctrf.json.\"\n  },\n  \"do_not_modify_enforced\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n    \"explanation\": \"The read-only constraint on /disk is enforced by Docker filesystem permissions.\"\n  },\n  \"binary_reward\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n    \"explanation\": \"tests/test.sh outputs strictly 1.0 or 0.0 to /logs/verifier/reward.txt.\"\n  }\n}\nEOF\n"]
